---
title: Rendering and Export
description: Render chart scenes through the default SVG renderer, the optional Canvas renderer, or a custom surface, then export supported output.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts compiles a renderer-neutral scene. The default renderer turns\nthat scene into accessible SVG markup; an optional Canvas renderer paints the\nsame scene through Canvas 2D. Both use the shared responsive, interaction,\ntooltip, keyboard, and runtime host."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the task-oriented "},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/exporting.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exporting guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to choose\nbetween static scene rendering, mounted SVG serialization, and raster output."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choose-a-renderer","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose a renderer"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer code stays behind explicit entry points:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default vanilla SVG host"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/dom"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vanilla Canvas host"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountCanvasChart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/canvas"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tween and spring SVG renderer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/motion"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer-neutral host"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/renderer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default React SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Preact SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/preact"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Vue SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/vue"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Solid SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/solid"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Svelte SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/svelte"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Angular SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/angular"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Lit SVG element"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/lit"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Alpine SVG directive"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"charts"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/alpine"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Native SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react-native"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Canvas component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react/canvas"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React custom-renderer component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react/core"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Octane SVG component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/octane"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane Canvas component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane custom-renderer component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/octane/core"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default package and adapter entries do not import Canvas. Applications pay\nfor it only when they import a Canvas entry. Motion is likewise isolated behind\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/motion"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/core"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter entries accept an explicit\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderer"},{"type":"text","value":" without choosing one for the application."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A default SVG host can still compose selected Canvas marks. Import\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" and attach it to those\nmarks. The default adapter remains the host, and the Canvas painter enters the\nmodule graph through that explicit import."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"react-native-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Native adapter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React Native adapter is experimental. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../installation.md#react-native-and-expo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for supported versions,\nverified checks, and native-device validation limits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React Native entry selects its native build through the package export\nconditions and renders the shared scene with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react-native-svg"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  Chart,\n  resolveNativePaint,\n  type NativeChartRenderContext,\n  type NativeChartTooltipRenderContext,\n  type NativePaintContext,\n  type NativePaintResolver,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react-native'\nimport {\n  tooltip,\n  type NativeChartTooltipComponent,\n  type NativeChartTooltipExtension,\n  type NativeChartTooltipProps,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react-native/tooltip'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NativeChartRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":" is passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRender"},{"type":"text","value":" callback.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NativeChartTooltipRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":" is passed to a custom tooltip renderer.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NativeChartTooltipProps"},{"type":"text","value":" describes the built-in native tooltip component,\nwhose component and extension contracts are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NativeChartTooltipComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NativeChartTooltipExtension"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveNativePaint"},{"type":"text","value":" as the default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NativePaintResolver"},{"type":"text","value":". It resolves\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"currentColor"},{"type":"text","value":", Canvas system colors, and CSS-variable fallbacks against a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NativePaintContext"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass a custom resolver through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" when the\napplication owns additional paint tokens."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"renderchartsvg","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/svg'\n\nconst markup = renderChartSvg(scene, {\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n  ariaDescription: 'Revenue increased through the second quarter.',\n  idPrefix: 'revenue',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function renderChartSvg(\n  scene: ChartScene,\n  options: RenderChartSvgOptions,\n): string\n\ninterface RenderChartSvgOptions {\n  ariaLabel: string\n  ariaDescription?: string\n  className?: string\n  tabIndex?: number\n  idPrefix?: string\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaLabel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessible SVG name"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaDescription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Escaped SVG "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<desc>"},{"type":"text","value":" content"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added after the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-chart"},{"type":"text","value":" class"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabIndex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG tab index for direct static rendering"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefix passed to renderers that generate document IDs"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The SVG uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role=\"img\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-roledescription=\"chart\""},{"type":"text","value":", a responsive\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width=\"100%\""},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height=\"100%\""},{"type":"text","value":", the scene's dimensions as its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"viewBox"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand an overflow-visible display style. A nontransparent scene background\nrenders as the first rect. All labels escape text and inherit the document\nfont."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus-filtered scene groups render hidden until the DOM host supplies focus\nstate. Data-less crosshair guides are also transient and are absent from this\nstatic serialization because no focus or cursor state was supplied. Scene keys\nbecome "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-ts-key"},{"type":"text","value":" attributes for reconciliation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"canvas-renderer","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canvas renderer"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { mountCanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(definition, { tooltip })\n\nconst host = mountCanvasChart(container, {\n  definition: interactiveDefinition,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountCanvasChart"},{"type":"text","value":" has the same definition, sizing, focus, spatial-index,\nkeyboard, tooltip, selection, update, and destroy behavior as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChart"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe renderer paints authored focus layers and crosshair guides below or above\nthe base scene on separate canvases, uses the browser device-pixel ratio by\ndefault, and maps pointer coordinates back into the scene."}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface CanvasChartRendererOptions {\n  pixelRatio?: number\n}\n\ninterface CanvasChartSurface<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> extends ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> {\n  readonly element: HTMLDivElement\n  readonly canvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly backgroundCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly focusUnderCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly sceneCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly focusCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n}\n\ninterface CanvasChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> extends ChartLayerRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> {\n  mount: (\n    container: HTMLElement,\n    requestRender: (force?: boolean) => void,\n  ) => CanvasChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ntype CanvasChartHostOptions<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> = Omit<ChartRendererHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>, 'renderer'>\n\ninterface CanvasChartHost<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  update: (options: CanvasChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>) => void\n  getScene: () => ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  destroy: () => void\n}\n\nfunction createCanvasChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  options?: CanvasChartRendererOptions,\n): CanvasChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n\nconst canvasChartRenderer: CanvasChartRenderer\n\nfunction mountCanvasChart<\n  TDatum,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  initialOptions: CanvasChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  runtime?: ChartRuntime<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): CanvasChartHost<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The surface's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"element"},{"type":"text","value":" is its accessible chart root. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" is the stable\nbase bitmap: chart background plus ordinary scene, without transient focus.\nIt remains suitable for direct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toBlob()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toDataURL()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls and is not\npart of the live visual stack. The live stack is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"backgroundCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusUnderCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sceneCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":". This lets an underlay\npaint above an opaque chart background but below ordinary marks without\nrepainting the stable base bitmap on cursor movement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A finite, positive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pixelRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" fixes every backing store at that ratio. An\nomitted value uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"devicePixelRatio"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":"; an invalid value uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CanvasChartHostOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" removes the required "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderer"},{"type":"text","value":" from the\nrenderer-neutral host options. The returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CanvasChartHost"},{"type":"text","value":" owns update,\nscene access, and cleanup. Its optional runtime parameter has the same advanced\nprerender-reuse contract as "},{"type":"link","href":"./dom-host.md#signature","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChart"}]},{"type":"text","value":", including\nruntime ownership on destroy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" for the shared default instance. Call\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCanvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" when the application needs a fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pixelRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" or\nan independently typed renderer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server-facing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prerender"},{"type":"text","value":" step emits a deterministic, named chart shell\nwith five "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":" canvases: the hidden stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" base bitmap plus\nthe public "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"backgroundCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusUnderCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sceneCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":" live layers. It does not attempt server-side pixel painting. The\nbrowser adopts that shell, sizes the backing stores, paints the scene, and\nattaches the shared interaction host. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR and Hydration"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canvas is an escape hatch for paint-heavy SVG output, not an unbounded-data\nmode. Scene compilation, channel arrays, scene nodes, and interaction points\nstill exist. A default nearest-point lookup remains linear unless the chart\nsupplies a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spatialIndex"},{"type":"text","value":"; measure the complete pipeline and bound or aggregate\noutput when pixels cannot distinguish the observations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer-specific tradeoffs:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canvas updates raster pixels instead of retaining one DOM element per scene\nnode."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canvas animation crossfades complete frames; SVG animation reconciles and\ninterpolates keyed elements."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Curved, polar, and geographic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" geometry requires browser "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Path2D"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SceneArea.polygons"},{"type":"text","value":" render directly and do not require "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Path2D"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scene-node "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" values do not create styleable Canvas descendants."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gradients require geometry with measurable bounds."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Radial gradients support Canvas fills only. A radial stroke throws rather\nthan changing stroke width under a nonuniform bounds transform."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Linear gradients map their normalized endpoints directly into each node's\nbounds. Radial fills are clipped to the node, then painted in normalized unit\nspace under the node's bounds transform. This preserves SVG\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"objectBoundingBox"},{"type":"text","value":" behavior, including an elliptical gradient on a non-square\nnode."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"svg-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG resources"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/svg'\nimport { renderChartSvgWithResources } from '@tanstack/charts/svg/resources'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" and the compatible explicit\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvgWithResources(scene, options)"},{"type":"text","value":" entry both:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"emit declared linear and radial gradients in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<defs>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scope gradient IDs with sanitized "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rewrite matching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"url(#gradient-id)"},{"type":"text","value":" paints"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"emit clip paths for scene groups with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clip"},{"type":"text","value":" bounds"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default SVG hosts and framework adapters use this behavior without a custom\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"},{"type":"text","value":". Use a stable, document-unique "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":". Gradient coordinates and\nstop offsets are clamped to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0..1"},{"type":"text","value":" and emitted as percentages. A radial\ngradient defaults to center "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(0.5, 0.5)"},{"type":"text","value":" and radius "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.5"},{"type":"text","value":"; each omitted focal\ncoordinate inherits the matching center coordinate."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React Native adapter emits matching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinearGradient"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RadialGradient"},{"type":"text","value":"\nresources through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react-native-svg"},{"type":"text","value":". Its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" generates an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":" with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useId()"},{"type":"text","value":" unless the application supplies one, then scopes resource IDs and\nrewrites matching paints in the same way as the web adapters."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reconcilechartsvg","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconcileChartSvg"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { reconcileChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/reconcile'\n\nconst cancel = reconcileChartSvg(container, nextMarkup, {\n  duration: 240,\n  easing: 'ease-out',\n})\n\ncancel()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function reconcileChartSvg(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  markup: string,\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions,\n): () => void","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The reconciler adopts a compatible existing root, matches children by\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-ts-key"},{"type":"text","value":", moves retained nodes into their new order, inserts entries, and\nremoves exits. When a node has no explicit key, same-tag sibling order is a\nfallback identity."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without animation, changed attributes and structure commit synchronously.\nWith animation:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"numeric attributes with compatible string structure interpolate"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"entries fade from zero opacity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"exits fade to zero and are then removed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"noninterpolable values commit immediately"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a returned cancellation function stops the current frame loop"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The DOM host calls reconciliation and cancellation for you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom SVG renderers that already own a keyed subtree can reconcile only that\nsubtree without reparsing or walking the surrounding chart:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { reconcileChartSvgFragment } from '@tanstack/charts/reconcile'\n\nconst cancel = reconcileChartSvgFragment(currentGroup, nextGroupMarkup, {\n  duration: 180,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function reconcileChartSvgFragment(\n  currentRoot: SVGElement,\n  markup: string,\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions,\n): () => void","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fragment root must keep the same namespace and element name to preserve\nits identity. Otherwise the reconciler replaces it. Child keying, tweening,\nand cancellation match "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconcileChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"animation-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Animation options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartAnimationOptions {\n  duration?: number\n  easing?:\n    | 'linear'\n    | 'ease'\n    | 'ease-in'\n    | 'ease-out'\n    | 'ease-in-out'\n    | ((progress: number) => number)\n  respectReducedMotion?: boolean\n  resize?: boolean\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"240"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Animation length in milliseconds, clamped to zero"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"easing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'ease-out'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Named built-in easing or a progress-mapping function"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"respectReducedMotion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lets a host suppress animation for reduced-motion mode"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Animates responsive and explicit host size changes"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On a definition, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation: true"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"240"},{"type":"text","value":" milliseconds, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ease-out"},{"type":"text","value":", and respects\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefers-reduced-motion: reduce"},{"type":"text","value":". A numeric duration is clamped to at least\nzero. A custom easing receives raw progress from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"respectReducedMotion"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resize"},{"type":"text","value":" are definition policies enforced by the\nhost. Direct\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconcileChartSvg(container, markup, animation)"},{"type":"text","value":" calls run the supplied\nanimation without consulting media queries or render reasons."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Host animation begins only after the initial render. Updates without a scene\nrender do not start an animation; the current animation options apply to the\nnext reconciliation. Responsive and explicit size changes commit immediately\nunless "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resize: true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark IDs and resolved datum identities are essential for meaningful\ntransitions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"svg-serialization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG serialization"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { downloadChartSvg, serializeChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/export'\n\nconst source = serializeChartSvg(container, {\n  width: 1200,\n  height: 600,\n  includeFocus: false,\n})\n\ndownloadChartSvg(container, 'revenue.svg')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The subpath exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serializeChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"downloadChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":", and the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SerializeChartSvgOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface SerializeChartSvgOptions {\n  width?: number\n  height?: number\n  includeFocus?: boolean\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"target"},{"type":"text","value":" may be the SVG or an ancestor containing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svg.ts-chart"},{"type":"text","value":". The serializer\nclones the SVG, adds the XML namespace, removes focus-filtered scene layers\nunless "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includeFocus"},{"type":"text","value":" is true, and resolves dimensions from options, then the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"viewBox"},{"type":"text","value":", then client dimensions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The serializer can inline computed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"},{"type":"text","value":", fill, fill opacity, font family,\nfont size, font weight, opacity, stroke, stroke opacity, stroke width, and\nstroke dash array when they depend on inherited font, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"currentColor"},{"type":"text","value":", or CSS\ncustom properties. Linear and radial resources remain in the cloned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<defs>"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand their stop color and opacity receive the same treatment. Keep other\nCSS-dependent resource styling explicit until it is part of that serialization\ncontract."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"downloadChartSvg(target, filename?, options?)"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chart.svg"},{"type":"text","value":" and\ndownloads an SVG blob through the target's document."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-image-export","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser image export"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { downloadChartImage, renderChartImage } from '@tanstack/charts/export'\n\nconst blob = await renderChartImage(container, {\n  type: 'image/webp',\n  scale: 2,\n  background: '#fff',\n  quality: 0.9,\n})\n\nawait downloadChartImage(container, 'revenue.png', {\n  scale: 2,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The browser image functions are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartImage"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"downloadChartImage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface RenderChartImageOptions extends SerializeChartSvgOptions {\n  scale?: number\n  background?: string\n  type?: 'image/png' | 'image/jpeg' | 'image/webp'\n  quality?: number\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Despite its historical name, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RenderChartImageOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" supports PNG, JPEG, and\nWebP. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scale"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2"},{"type":"text","value":" and is clamped to at least "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.1"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image/png"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Encoding support depends on the browser. If the requested encoder is\nunavailable, the browser can return PNG instead, including WebP requests in\nWebKit. Check the returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blob.type"},{"type":"text","value":" before choosing a filename or sending\nthe image to a consumer that requires a specific format."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raster export requires:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a browser document and window"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nonzero chart dimensions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canvas 2D"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"successful browser decoding when the source is SVG"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The promise rejects when any requirement fails or Canvas encoding returns no\nblob. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"downloadChartImage"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chart.png"},{"type":"text","value":"; keep the filename extension\nconsistent with the actual encoded MIME type. The download helper uses the\nfilename you supply and does not rename it after an encoding fallback."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The raster helpers accept a mounted SVG, Canvas, or mixed chart root, or an\nancestor containing one. SVG is serialized, decoded, and drawn into the export\ncanvas. Canvas uses the stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" base bitmap directly when focus is\nexcluded. With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includeFocus"},{"type":"text","value":", it composites "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"backgroundCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusUnderCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sceneCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusCanvas"},{"type":"text","value":" in that order. Mixed roots\ndraw every child surface in visual order. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serializeChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"downloadChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" reject mixed roots and remain SVG-only."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mark-level-renderers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mark-level renderers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Cartesian, radial, and composite marks accept a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderer"},{"type":"text","value":" option.\nPassing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" opts that mark into Canvas while axes, guides,\nand marks without the option keep the host renderer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { areaY, defineChart, lineY, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { canvasChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(denseRows, {\n      x: 'time',\n      y: 'value',\n      renderer: canvasChartRenderer,\n    }),\n    lineY(summaryRows, { x: 'time', y: 'value' }),\n    text(labels, { x: 'time', y: 'value', text: 'label' }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adjacent nodes with the same renderer share a layer. Alternating renderer runs\nremain in declaration order, including nested runs inside facets, composites,\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"polar"},{"type":"text","value":". Server output contains one accessible mixed root with\ndeterministic child shells, and the browser adopts those shells. Direct\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg(scene, options)"},{"type":"text","value":" calls remain an explicit SVG serialization of\nthe complete renderer-neutral scene and do not run surface composition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The universal mark contract stays small:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartMarkRenderer {\n  readonly kind: 'chart-layer-renderer'\n  readonly id: string\n}\n\ninterface ChartMarkOptions {\n  renderer?: ChartMarkRenderer\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A renderer that mounts one DOM layer implements the complete composition\ncontract:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartLayerRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>\n  extends ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>, ChartMarkRenderer {\n  compose: (\n    defaultRenderer: ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  ) => ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ninterface UniversalChartLayerRenderer\n  extends UniversalChartRenderer, ChartMarkRenderer {\n  compose: (\n    defaultRenderer: ChartRenderer<any, any, any>,\n  ) => ChartRenderer<any, any, any>\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first non-default mark renderer supplies the compositor. The built-in\nCanvas renderer can compose normal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" surfaces and exposes the\nresult as one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurface"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mark motion and renderer selection are independent in the authoring API. The\nbuilt-in factories preserve both options, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMark"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps motion as its\nsecond argument and accepts the renderer as its third. The optional\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" renderer consumes tween and spring policy only on layers it owns.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" paints the final mark scene and does not interpret that\npolicy. A host "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation"},{"type":"text","value":" can still crossfade complete Canvas frames while\nSVG layers reconcile keyed elements. Changing the layer renderer sequence\nremounts the composition, so that structural update does not animate between\nthe old and new surface layout."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-renderers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom renderers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The renderer-neutral boundary consists of a renderer instance contract and\nthe mounted surface it returns:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartSurfaceRenderOptions extends RenderChartOptions {\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions\n}\n\ninterface ChartSurface<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly renderer: ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  readonly element: Element\n  readonly layers?: readonly ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[]\n  readonly defaultElement?: Element\n  render: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    options: ChartSurfaceRenderOptions,\n  ) => void\n  clientToScene?: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    clientX: number,\n    clientY: number,\n  ) => { x: number; y: number } | null\n  getPresentationPoints?: () =>\n    readonly ChartPoint<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[] | undefined\n  subscribePresentationPoints?: (\n    listener: (points: readonly ChartPoint<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[]) => void,\n  ) => () => void\n  paintFocus: (\n    focus: ChartFocusState<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> | null,\n    pointer?: ChartTooltipPosition | null,\n    cursor?: ChartCursorPresentation<TXValue, TYValue> | null,\n    options?: { stateFocus: ChartFocusState<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> | null },\n  ) => ChartScene | void\n  readonly supportsStateFocus?: true\n  destroy: () => void\n}\n\ninterface ChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly id: string\n  readonly capabilities?: ChartRendererCapabilities\n  prerender: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    options: RenderChartOptions,\n  ) => string\n  mount: (\n    container: HTMLElement,\n    requestRender: (force?: boolean) => void,\n  ) => ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ninterface ChartRendererRenderContext<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  container: HTMLElement\n  scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  surface: ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"element"},{"type":"text","value":" is the one accessible, interactive root. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"surface.destroy()"},{"type":"text","value":" releases animation work,\nsubscriptions, and renderer resources. The mounting host owns removal of the\nchart root and cleanup of its interaction listeners."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layers"},{"type":"text","value":", when present,\nlists child surfaces from back to front. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultElement"},{"type":"text","value":" is the topmost\nsurface element owned by the host's default renderer. SVG-oriented\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks expose that element as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svg"},{"type":"text","value":" and also include\nthe complete renderer-neutral "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"surface"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes\nthe complete surface directly."}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartRenderContext<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  container: HTMLElement\n  svg: SVGSVGElement\n  scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  surface: ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Member"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsibility"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRenderer.id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable renderer identifier"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRenderer.capabilities"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expose optional versioned services that the shared host injects into extensions"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prerender()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return deterministic accessible markup for the supplied scene and render options"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mount()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adopt or create a surface in the container and connect renderer-owned environment observers"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurface.renderer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refer to the renderer that created the surface; a different renderer object on update replaces the surface"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurface.element"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expose the accessible, focusable root used by shared keyboard and focus handling"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurface.layers"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expose ordered child surfaces when this surface composes more than one renderer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurface.defaultElement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expose the topmost element owned by the host's default renderer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paint the complete scene and apply accessible name, class, tab index, ID prefix, and optional animation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientToScene()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optionally convert viewport client coordinates to scene coordinates; the controller returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" when omitted or unavailable"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPresentationPoints()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expose renderer-owned point geometry while a scene transition is active"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribePresentationPoints()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notify the host as presentation geometry advances so focus and tooltips remain aligned"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paintFocus()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paint or clear authored focus layers and guides, then optionally return the destination scene used for subsequent pointer hits"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destroy()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Release renderer-owned animation, observers, listeners, and resources"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rectangle-geometry-helpers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rectangle geometry helpers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom rectangle renderers can share the built-in corner-fit policy:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  rectCornerRadiiPath,\n  resolveRectCornerRadii,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/renderer/rect'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveRectCornerRadii(corners, width, height)"},{"type":"text","value":" changes invalid or negative\nvalues to zero and proportionally fits adjacent radii within the rectangle.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rectCornerRadiiPath(x, y, width, height, corners)"},{"type":"text","value":" serializes the same\nnormalized geometry as a stable SVG path. The helper accepts reversed width or\nheight and keeps the tuple in physical corner order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestRender()"},{"type":"text","value":" asks the shared host to rebuild and repaint on its next\nanimation frame; ordinary requests proceed only when a container-owned width\nor height changed.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestRender(true)"},{"type":"text","value":" forces the work when renderer state changed without a\nwidth or chart-option change, such as device-pixel ratio or resolved theme\ncolors. Requests made before the same frame are coalesced."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer capabilities are structural so independently bundled package\nentrypoints do not need shared object or symbol identity. A renderer can expose\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"capabilities.tooltipMotion"},{"type":"text","value":" with protocol "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":"; the host creates its controller\nand injects it as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipExtensionContext.motion"},{"type":"text","value":". Renderers that omit the\ncapability do not load or run tooltip motion code."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Animated renderers can expose their current point geometry through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPresentationPoints()"},{"type":"text","value":" and notify the host through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribePresentationPoints()"},{"type":"text","value":". The host then resolves stationary pointers,\npinned tooltips, and keyboard focus against the painted positions rather than\nthe destination scene."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When focus activates inline mark-state geometry, return the resolved scene that\nthe surface paints. The host uses that destination scene for subsequent\npointer resolution while the renderer animates toward it. Returning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":"\nkeeps the base scene as the interaction source and remains valid for renderers\nthat do not resolve alternate scene geometry."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom surfaces can reuse the environment-safe focus lifecycle exported from\nthe root and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/universal"},{"type":"text","value":" entries:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const focusedScene = resolveFocusScene(scene, focus).scene\nconst under = focusedSceneNodes(focusedScene, focus, 'under')\nconst over = focusedSceneNodes(focusedScene, focus, 'over')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveFocusScene"},{"type":"text","value":" materializes retargetable focus candidates under stable\nkeys. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusedSceneNodes"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the ordinary nodes for the requested paint\nplacement. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveFocusPresentation(scene, focus, pointer, cursor)"},{"type":"text","value":" applies\nthat lifecycle and returns renderer-neutral "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"under"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"over"},{"type":"text","value":" nodes. Paint\nthem in this order: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"under"},{"type":"text","value":", the base scene, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"over"},{"type":"text","value":". The optional cursor\nargument is the controller state projected into this surface's plot and can\ndrive a crosshair without datum focus. This is the same path used by the SVG,\nCanvas, and React Native surfaces."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared host continues to own runtime updates, responsive sizing, text\nmeasurement, focus resolution, keyboard behavior, built-in tooltips, selection,\nand callbacks. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":" reports the live "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"surface"},{"type":"text","value":" and the\nstable interaction controller instead of assuming an SVG element."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/renderer"},{"type":"text","value":", or the React and\nOctane "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/core"},{"type":"text","value":" entries, to mount a custom renderer. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RenderChartOptions"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurfaceRenderOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurface"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererCapabilities"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererTooltipMotionCapability"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipMotionController"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipMotionSnapshot"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererHostCommonOptions"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererHostOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererHost"},{"type":"text","value":" describe the complete\nboundary."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/renderer"},{"type":"text","value":" when implementing\na host outside the shared adapters. The function returns the effective renderer\nfor prerendering or mounting a scene. It returns the default when every node\nuses that renderer. Otherwise it asks the first non-default\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartLayerRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" to compose the ordered layers with the default renderer.\nThe shared DOM host and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChartRendererAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" perform this resolution\nautomatically."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG remains available as a renderer implementation:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createSvgChartRenderer,\n  svgChartRenderer,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/svg/renderer'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function createSvgChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  renderSvg?: ChartSvgRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n\nconst svgChartRenderer: ChartRenderer","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSvgChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" adapts a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSvgRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" into a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":".\nOmitting the argument uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" is the shared\npreconfigured instance for renderer-neutral hosts that want the built-in SVG\nsurface.\nPass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSvgRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" to the compatibility SVG host or\ndefault framework adapter when only SVG serialization needs to change. Such a\nrenderer should preserve:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"an SVG root discoverable by the host"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-ts-key"},{"type":"text","value":" identities for reconciliation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"focus-filtered scene groups and data-less guides when chart-owned focus paint is\ndesired"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the scene coordinate system and accessible name"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom-extensions.md#custom-renderers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom extensions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" before\nreplacing the shared renderer."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"choose-a-renderer","text":"Choose a renderer","level":2},{"id":"react-native-adapter","text":"React Native adapter","level":2},{"id":"renderchartsvg","text":"renderChartSvg","level":2},{"id":"canvas-renderer","text":"Canvas renderer","level":2},{"id":"svg-resources","text":"SVG resources","level":2},{"id":"reconcilechartsvg","text":"reconcileChartSvg","level":2},{"id":"animation-options","text":"Animation options","level":2},{"id":"svg-serialization","text":"SVG serialization","level":2},{"id":"browser-image-export","text":"Browser image export","level":2},{"id":"mark-level-renderers","text":"Mark-level renderers","level":2},{"id":"custom-renderers","text":"Custom renderers","level":2},{"id":"rectangle-geometry-helpers","text":"Rectangle geometry helpers","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Charts compiles a renderer-neutral scene. The default renderer turns\nthat scene into accessible SVG markup; an optional Canvas renderer paints the\nsame scene through Canvas 2D. Both use the shared responsive, interaction,\ntooltip, keyboard, and runtime host.\n\nUse the task-oriented [Exporting guide](../guides/exporting.md) to choose\nbetween static scene rendering, mounted SVG serialization, and raster output.\n\n## Choose a renderer\n\nRenderer code stays behind explicit entry points:\n\n| Use                              | Import                                                |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Default vanilla SVG host         | `mountChart` from `@tanstack/charts/dom`              |\n| Vanilla Canvas host              | `mountCanvasChart` from `@tanstack/charts/canvas`     |\n| Tween and spring SVG renderer    | `motion` from `@tanstack/charts/motion`               |\n| Renderer-neutral host            | `mountChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/renderer` |\n| Default React SVG component      | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react`                 |\n| Default Preact SVG component     | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/preact`                |\n| Default Vue SVG component        | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/vue`                   |\n| Default Solid SVG component      | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/solid`                 |\n| Default Svelte SVG component     | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/svelte`                |\n| Default Angular SVG component    | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/angular`               |\n| Default Lit SVG element          | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/lit`                   |\n| Default Alpine SVG directive     | `charts` from `@tanstack/charts/alpine`               |\n| React Native SVG component       | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react-native`          |\n| React Canvas component           | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react/canvas`          |\n| React custom-renderer component  | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react/core`            |\n| Default Octane SVG component     | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/octane`                |\n| Octane Canvas component          | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas`         |\n| Octane custom-renderer component | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/octane/core`           |\n\nThe default package and adapter entries do not import Canvas. Applications pay\nfor it only when they import a Canvas entry. Motion is likewise isolated behind\n`@tanstack/charts/motion`. The `/core` adapter entries accept an explicit\n`renderer` without choosing one for the application.\n\nA default SVG host can still compose selected Canvas marks. Import\n`canvasChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/canvas` and attach it to those\nmarks. The default adapter remains the host, and the Canvas painter enters the\nmodule graph through that explicit import.\n\n## React Native adapter\n\nThe React Native adapter is experimental. See\n[Installation](../installation.md#react-native-and-expo) for supported versions,\nverified checks, and native-device validation limits.\n\nThe React Native entry selects its native build through the package export\nconditions and renders the shared scene with `react-native-svg`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  Chart,\n  resolveNativePaint,\n  type NativeChartRenderContext,\n  type NativeChartTooltipRenderContext,\n  type NativePaintContext,\n  type NativePaintResolver,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react-native'\nimport {\n  tooltip,\n  type NativeChartTooltipComponent,\n  type NativeChartTooltipExtension,\n  type NativeChartTooltipProps,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react-native/tooltip'\n```\n\n`NativeChartRenderContext` is passed to `Chart`'s `onRender` callback.\n`NativeChartTooltipRenderContext` is passed to a custom tooltip renderer.\n`NativeChartTooltipProps` describes the built-in native tooltip component,\nwhose component and extension contracts are `NativeChartTooltipComponent` and\n`NativeChartTooltipExtension`.\n\nUse `resolveNativePaint` as the default `NativePaintResolver`. It resolves\n`currentColor`, Canvas system colors, and CSS-variable fallbacks against a\n`NativePaintContext`. Pass a custom resolver through `Chart` when the\napplication owns additional paint tokens.\n\n## `renderChartSvg`\n\n```ts\nimport { renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/svg'\n\nconst markup = renderChartSvg(scene, {\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n  ariaDescription: 'Revenue increased through the second quarter.',\n  idPrefix: 'revenue',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction renderChartSvg(\n  scene: ChartScene,\n  options: RenderChartSvgOptions,\n): string\n\ninterface RenderChartSvgOptions {\n  ariaLabel: string\n  ariaDescription?: string\n  className?: string\n  tabIndex?: number\n  idPrefix?: string\n}\n```\n\n| Option            | Default  | Meaning                                               |\n| ----------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ariaLabel`       | Required | Accessible SVG name                                   |\n| `ariaDescription` | None     | Escaped SVG `<desc>` content                          |\n| `className`       | None     | Added after the `ts-chart` class                      |\n| `tabIndex`        | `0`      | SVG tab index for direct static rendering             |\n| `idPrefix`        | Empty    | Prefix passed to renderers that generate document IDs |\n\nThe SVG uses `role=\"img\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"chart\"`, a responsive\n`width=\"100%\"` and `height=\"100%\"`, the scene's dimensions as its `viewBox`,\nand an overflow-visible display style. A nontransparent scene background\nrenders as the first rect. All labels escape text and inherit the document\nfont.\n\nFocus-filtered scene groups render hidden until the DOM host supplies focus\nstate. Data-less crosshair guides are also transient and are absent from this\nstatic serialization because no focus or cursor state was supplied. Scene keys\nbecome `data-ts-key` attributes for reconciliation.\n\n## Canvas renderer\n\n```ts\nimport { mountCanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(definition, { tooltip })\n\nconst host = mountCanvasChart(container, {\n  definition: interactiveDefinition,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n})\n```\n\n`mountCanvasChart` has the same definition, sizing, focus, spatial-index,\nkeyboard, tooltip, selection, update, and destroy behavior as `mountChart`.\nThe renderer paints authored focus layers and crosshair guides below or above\nthe base scene on separate canvases, uses the browser device-pixel ratio by\ndefault, and maps pointer coordinates back into the scene.\n\n```ts\ninterface CanvasChartRendererOptions {\n  pixelRatio?: number\n}\n\ninterface CanvasChartSurface<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> extends ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> {\n  readonly element: HTMLDivElement\n  readonly canvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly backgroundCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly focusUnderCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly sceneCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly focusCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n}\n\ninterface CanvasChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> extends ChartLayerRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> {\n  mount: (\n    container: HTMLElement,\n    requestRender: (force?: boolean) => void,\n  ) => CanvasChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ntype CanvasChartHostOptions<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> = Omit<ChartRendererHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>, 'renderer'>\n\ninterface CanvasChartHost<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  update: (options: CanvasChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>) => void\n  getScene: () => ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  destroy: () => void\n}\n\nfunction createCanvasChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  options?: CanvasChartRendererOptions,\n): CanvasChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n\nconst canvasChartRenderer: CanvasChartRenderer\n\nfunction mountCanvasChart<\n  TDatum,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  initialOptions: CanvasChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  runtime?: ChartRuntime<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): CanvasChartHost<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n```\n\nThe surface's `element` is its accessible chart root. `canvas` is the stable\nbase bitmap: chart background plus ordinary scene, without transient focus.\nIt remains suitable for direct `toBlob()` and `toDataURL()` calls and is not\npart of the live visual stack. The live stack is `backgroundCanvas`,\n`focusUnderCanvas`, `sceneCanvas`, then `focusCanvas`. This lets an underlay\npaint above an opaque chart background but below ordinary marks without\nrepainting the stable base bitmap on cursor movement.\n\nA finite, positive `pixelRatio` fixes every backing store at that ratio. An\nomitted value uses `devicePixelRatio`, then `1`; an invalid value uses `1`.\n\n`CanvasChartHostOptions` removes the required `renderer` from the\nrenderer-neutral host options. The returned `CanvasChartHost` owns update,\nscene access, and cleanup. Its optional runtime parameter has the same advanced\nprerender-reuse contract as [`mountChart`](./dom-host.md#signature), including\nruntime ownership on destroy.\n\nUse `canvasChartRenderer` for the shared default instance. Call\n`createCanvasChartRenderer` when the application needs a fixed `pixelRatio` or\nan independently typed renderer instance.\n\nThe server-facing `prerender` step emits a deterministic, named chart shell\nwith five `aria-hidden` canvases: the hidden stable `canvas` base bitmap plus\nthe public `backgroundCanvas`, `focusUnderCanvas`, `sceneCanvas`, and\n`focusCanvas` live layers. It does not attempt server-side pixel painting. The\nbrowser adopts that shell, sizes the backing stores, paints the scene, and\nattaches the shared interaction host. See\n[SSR and Hydration](../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md).\n\nCanvas is an escape hatch for paint-heavy SVG output, not an unbounded-data\nmode. Scene compilation, channel arrays, scene nodes, and interaction points\nstill exist. A default nearest-point lookup remains linear unless the chart\nsupplies a `spatialIndex`; measure the complete pipeline and bound or aggregate\noutput when pixels cannot distinguish the observations.\n\nRenderer-specific tradeoffs:\n\n- Canvas updates raster pixels instead of retaining one DOM element per scene\n  node.\n- Canvas animation crossfades complete frames; SVG animation reconciles and\n  interpolates keyed elements.\n- Curved, polar, and geographic `path` geometry requires browser `Path2D`.\n- Structured `SceneArea.polygons` render directly and do not require `Path2D`.\n- Scene-node `className` values do not create styleable Canvas descendants.\n- Gradients require geometry with measurable bounds.\n- Radial gradients support Canvas fills only. A radial stroke throws rather\n  than changing stroke width under a nonuniform bounds transform.\n\nLinear gradients map their normalized endpoints directly into each node's\nbounds. Radial fills are clipped to the node, then painted in normalized unit\nspace under the node's bounds transform. This preserves SVG\n`objectBoundingBox` behavior, including an elliptical gradient on a non-square\nnode.\n\n## SVG resources\n\n```ts\nimport { renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/svg'\nimport { renderChartSvgWithResources } from '@tanstack/charts/svg/resources'\n```\n\n`renderChartSvg` and the compatible explicit\n`renderChartSvgWithResources(scene, options)` entry both:\n\n- emit declared linear and radial gradients in `<defs>`\n- scope gradient IDs with sanitized `idPrefix`\n- rewrite matching `url(#gradient-id)` paints\n- emit clip paths for scene groups with `clip` bounds\n\nDefault SVG hosts and framework adapters use this behavior without a custom\n`renderSvg`. Use a stable, document-unique `idPrefix`. Gradient coordinates and\nstop offsets are clamped to `0..1` and emitted as percentages. A radial\ngradient defaults to center `(0.5, 0.5)` and radius `0.5`; each omitted focal\ncoordinate inherits the matching center coordinate.\n\nThe React Native adapter emits matching `LinearGradient` and `RadialGradient`\nresources through `react-native-svg`. Its `Chart` generates an `idPrefix` with\n`useId()` unless the application supplies one, then scopes resource IDs and\nrewrites matching paints in the same way as the web adapters.\n\n## `reconcileChartSvg`\n\n```ts\nimport { reconcileChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/reconcile'\n\nconst cancel = reconcileChartSvg(container, nextMarkup, {\n  duration: 240,\n  easing: 'ease-out',\n})\n\ncancel()\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction reconcileChartSvg(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  markup: string,\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions,\n): () => void\n```\n\nThe reconciler adopts a compatible existing root, matches children by\n`data-ts-key`, moves retained nodes into their new order, inserts entries, and\nremoves exits. When a node has no explicit key, same-tag sibling order is a\nfallback identity.\n\nWithout animation, changed attributes and structure commit synchronously.\nWith animation:\n\n- numeric attributes with compatible string structure interpolate\n- entries fade from zero opacity\n- exits fade to zero and are then removed\n- noninterpolable values commit immediately\n- a returned cancellation function stops the current frame loop\n\nThe DOM host calls reconciliation and cancellation for you.\n\nCustom SVG renderers that already own a keyed subtree can reconcile only that\nsubtree without reparsing or walking the surrounding chart:\n\n```ts\nimport { reconcileChartSvgFragment } from '@tanstack/charts/reconcile'\n\nconst cancel = reconcileChartSvgFragment(currentGroup, nextGroupMarkup, {\n  duration: 180,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction reconcileChartSvgFragment(\n  currentRoot: SVGElement,\n  markup: string,\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions,\n): () => void\n```\n\nThe fragment root must keep the same namespace and element name to preserve\nits identity. Otherwise the reconciler replaces it. Child keying, tweening,\nand cancellation match `reconcileChartSvg`.\n\n## Animation options\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartAnimationOptions {\n  duration?: number\n  easing?:\n    | 'linear'\n    | 'ease'\n    | 'ease-in'\n    | 'ease-out'\n    | 'ease-in-out'\n    | ((progress: number) => number)\n  respectReducedMotion?: boolean\n  resize?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n| Option                 | Default      | Meaning                                                |\n| ---------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `duration`             | `240`        | Animation length in milliseconds, clamped to zero      |\n| `easing`               | `'ease-out'` | Named built-in easing or a progress-mapping function   |\n| `respectReducedMotion` | `true`       | Lets a host suppress animation for reduced-motion mode |\n| `resize`               | `false`      | Animates responsive and explicit host size changes     |\n\nOn a definition, `svgAnimation: true` uses `240` milliseconds, `ease-out`, and respects\n`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. A numeric duration is clamped to at least\nzero. A custom easing receives raw progress from `0` to `1`.\n\n`respectReducedMotion` and `resize` are definition policies enforced by the\nhost. Direct\n`reconcileChartSvg(container, markup, animation)` calls run the supplied\nanimation without consulting media queries or render reasons.\n\nHost animation begins only after the initial render. Updates without a scene\nrender do not start an animation; the current animation options apply to the\nnext reconciliation. Responsive and explicit size changes commit immediately\nunless `resize: true`.\n\nStable mark IDs and resolved datum identities are essential for meaningful\ntransitions.\n\n## SVG serialization\n\n```ts\nimport { downloadChartSvg, serializeChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/export'\n\nconst source = serializeChartSvg(container, {\n  width: 1200,\n  height: 600,\n  includeFocus: false,\n})\n\ndownloadChartSvg(container, 'revenue.svg')\n```\n\nThe subpath exports `serializeChartSvg`, `downloadChartSvg`, and the\n`SerializeChartSvgOptions` type.\n\n```ts\ninterface SerializeChartSvgOptions {\n  width?: number\n  height?: number\n  includeFocus?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n`target` may be the SVG or an ancestor containing `svg.ts-chart`. The serializer\nclones the SVG, adds the XML namespace, removes focus-filtered scene layers\nunless `includeFocus` is true, and resolves dimensions from options, then the\n`viewBox`, then client dimensions.\n\nThe serializer can inline computed `color`, fill, fill opacity, font family,\nfont size, font weight, opacity, stroke, stroke opacity, stroke width, and\nstroke dash array when they depend on inherited font, `currentColor`, or CSS\ncustom properties. Linear and radial resources remain in the cloned `<defs>`,\nand their stop color and opacity receive the same treatment. Keep other\nCSS-dependent resource styling explicit until it is part of that serialization\ncontract.\n\n`downloadChartSvg(target, filename?, options?)` defaults to `chart.svg` and\ndownloads an SVG blob through the target's document.\n\n## Browser image export\n\n```ts\nimport { downloadChartImage, renderChartImage } from '@tanstack/charts/export'\n\nconst blob = await renderChartImage(container, {\n  type: 'image/webp',\n  scale: 2,\n  background: '#fff',\n  quality: 0.9,\n})\n\nawait downloadChartImage(container, 'revenue.png', {\n  scale: 2,\n})\n```\n\nThe browser image functions are `renderChartImage` and\n`downloadChartImage`.\n\n```ts\ninterface RenderChartImageOptions extends SerializeChartSvgOptions {\n  scale?: number\n  background?: string\n  type?: 'image/png' | 'image/jpeg' | 'image/webp'\n  quality?: number\n}\n```\n\nDespite its historical name, `RenderChartImageOptions` supports PNG, JPEG, and\nWebP. `scale` defaults to `2` and is clamped to at least `0.1`. `type` defaults\nto `image/png`.\n\nEncoding support depends on the browser. If the requested encoder is\nunavailable, the browser can return PNG instead, including WebP requests in\nWebKit. Check the returned `blob.type` before choosing a filename or sending\nthe image to a consumer that requires a specific format.\n\nRaster export requires:\n\n- a browser document and window\n- nonzero chart dimensions\n- Canvas 2D\n- successful browser decoding when the source is SVG\n\nThe promise rejects when any requirement fails or Canvas encoding returns no\nblob. `downloadChartImage` defaults to `chart.png`; keep the filename extension\nconsistent with the actual encoded MIME type. The download helper uses the\nfilename you supply and does not rename it after an encoding fallback.\n\nThe raster helpers accept a mounted SVG, Canvas, or mixed chart root, or an\nancestor containing one. SVG is serialized, decoded, and drawn into the export\ncanvas. Canvas uses the stable `canvas` base bitmap directly when focus is\nexcluded. With `includeFocus`, it composites `backgroundCanvas`,\n`focusUnderCanvas`, `sceneCanvas`, and `focusCanvas` in that order. Mixed roots\ndraw every child surface in visual order. `serializeChartSvg` and\n`downloadChartSvg` reject mixed roots and remain SVG-only.\n\n## Mark-level renderers\n\nBuilt-in Cartesian, radial, and composite marks accept a `renderer` option.\nPassing `canvasChartRenderer` opts that mark into Canvas while axes, guides,\nand marks without the option keep the host renderer:\n\n```ts\nimport { areaY, defineChart, lineY, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { canvasChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(denseRows, {\n      x: 'time',\n      y: 'value',\n      renderer: canvasChartRenderer,\n    }),\n    lineY(summaryRows, { x: 'time', y: 'value' }),\n    text(labels, { x: 'time', y: 'value', text: 'label' }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nAdjacent nodes with the same renderer share a layer. Alternating renderer runs\nremain in declaration order, including nested runs inside facets, composites,\nand `polar`. Server output contains one accessible mixed root with\ndeterministic child shells, and the browser adopts those shells. Direct\n`renderChartSvg(scene, options)` calls remain an explicit SVG serialization of\nthe complete renderer-neutral scene and do not run surface composition.\n\nThe universal mark contract stays small:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartMarkRenderer {\n  readonly kind: 'chart-layer-renderer'\n  readonly id: string\n}\n\ninterface ChartMarkOptions {\n  renderer?: ChartMarkRenderer\n}\n```\n\nA renderer that mounts one DOM layer implements the complete composition\ncontract:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartLayerRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>\n  extends ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>, ChartMarkRenderer {\n  compose: (\n    defaultRenderer: ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  ) => ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ninterface UniversalChartLayerRenderer\n  extends UniversalChartRenderer, ChartMarkRenderer {\n  compose: (\n    defaultRenderer: ChartRenderer<any, any, any>,\n  ) => ChartRenderer<any, any, any>\n}\n```\n\nThe first non-default mark renderer supplies the compositor. The built-in\nCanvas renderer can compose normal `ChartRenderer` surfaces and exposes the\nresult as one `ChartSurface`.\n\nMark motion and renderer selection are independent in the authoring API. The\nbuilt-in factories preserve both options, and `createMark` keeps motion as its\nsecond argument and accepts the renderer as its third. The optional\n`motion()` renderer consumes tween and spring policy only on layers it owns.\n`canvasChartRenderer` paints the final mark scene and does not interpret that\npolicy. A host `svgAnimation` can still crossfade complete Canvas frames while\nSVG layers reconcile keyed elements. Changing the layer renderer sequence\nremounts the composition, so that structural update does not animate between\nthe old and new surface layout.\n\n## Custom renderers\n\nThe renderer-neutral boundary consists of a renderer instance contract and\nthe mounted surface it returns:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartSurfaceRenderOptions extends RenderChartOptions {\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions\n}\n\ninterface ChartSurface<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly renderer: ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  readonly element: Element\n  readonly layers?: readonly ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[]\n  readonly defaultElement?: Element\n  render: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    options: ChartSurfaceRenderOptions,\n  ) => void\n  clientToScene?: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    clientX: number,\n    clientY: number,\n  ) => { x: number; y: number } | null\n  getPresentationPoints?: () =>\n    readonly ChartPoint<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[] | undefined\n  subscribePresentationPoints?: (\n    listener: (points: readonly ChartPoint<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[]) => void,\n  ) => () => void\n  paintFocus: (\n    focus: ChartFocusState<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> | null,\n    pointer?: ChartTooltipPosition | null,\n    cursor?: ChartCursorPresentation<TXValue, TYValue> | null,\n    options?: { stateFocus: ChartFocusState<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> | null },\n  ) => ChartScene | void\n  readonly supportsStateFocus?: true\n  destroy: () => void\n}\n\ninterface ChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly id: string\n  readonly capabilities?: ChartRendererCapabilities\n  prerender: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    options: RenderChartOptions,\n  ) => string\n  mount: (\n    container: HTMLElement,\n    requestRender: (force?: boolean) => void,\n  ) => ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ninterface ChartRendererRenderContext<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  container: HTMLElement\n  scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  surface: ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n```\n\n`element` is the one accessible, interactive root. `surface.destroy()` releases animation work,\nsubscriptions, and renderer resources. The mounting host owns removal of the\nchart root and cleanup of its interaction listeners.\n\n`layers`, when present,\nlists child surfaces from back to front. `defaultElement` is the topmost\nsurface element owned by the host's default renderer. SVG-oriented\n`ChartRenderContext` callbacks expose that element as `svg` and also include\nthe complete renderer-neutral `surface`. `ChartRendererRenderContext` exposes\nthe complete surface directly.\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartRenderContext<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  container: HTMLElement\n  svg: SVGSVGElement\n  scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  surface: ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n```\n\n| Member                          | Responsibility                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ChartRenderer.id`              | Stable renderer identifier                                                                                                     |\n| `ChartRenderer.capabilities`    | Expose optional versioned services that the shared host injects into extensions                                                |\n| `prerender()`                   | Return deterministic accessible markup for the supplied scene and render options                                               |\n| `mount()`                       | Adopt or create a surface in the container and connect renderer-owned environment observers                                    |\n| `ChartSurface.renderer`         | Refer to the renderer that created the surface; a different renderer object on update replaces the surface                     |\n| `ChartSurface.element`          | Expose the accessible, focusable root used by shared keyboard and focus handling                                               |\n| `ChartSurface.layers`           | Expose ordered child surfaces when this surface composes more than one renderer                                                |\n| `ChartSurface.defaultElement`   | Expose the topmost element owned by the host's default renderer                                                                |\n| `render()`                      | Paint the complete scene and apply accessible name, class, tab index, ID prefix, and optional animation                        |\n| `clientToScene()`               | Optionally convert viewport client coordinates to scene coordinates; the controller returns `null` when omitted or unavailable |\n| `getPresentationPoints()`       | Expose renderer-owned point geometry while a scene transition is active                                                        |\n| `subscribePresentationPoints()` | Notify the host as presentation geometry advances so focus and tooltips remain aligned                                         |\n| `paintFocus()`                  | Paint or clear authored focus layers and guides, then optionally return the destination scene used for subsequent pointer hits |\n| `destroy()`                     | Release renderer-owned animation, observers, listeners, and resources                                                          |\n\n### Rectangle geometry helpers\n\nCustom rectangle renderers can share the built-in corner-fit policy:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  rectCornerRadiiPath,\n  resolveRectCornerRadii,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/renderer/rect'\n```\n\n`resolveRectCornerRadii(corners, width, height)` changes invalid or negative\nvalues to zero and proportionally fits adjacent radii within the rectangle.\n`rectCornerRadiiPath(x, y, width, height, corners)` serializes the same\nnormalized geometry as a stable SVG path. The helper accepts reversed width or\nheight and keeps the tuple in physical corner order.\n\n`requestRender()` asks the shared host to rebuild and repaint on its next\nanimation frame; ordinary requests proceed only when a container-owned width\nor height changed.\n`requestRender(true)` forces the work when renderer state changed without a\nwidth or chart-option change, such as device-pixel ratio or resolved theme\ncolors. Requests made before the same frame are coalesced.\n\nRenderer capabilities are structural so independently bundled package\nentrypoints do not need shared object or symbol identity. A renderer can expose\n`capabilities.tooltipMotion` with protocol `1`; the host creates its controller\nand injects it as `ChartTooltipExtensionContext.motion`. Renderers that omit the\ncapability do not load or run tooltip motion code.\n\nAnimated renderers can expose their current point geometry through\n`getPresentationPoints()` and notify the host through\n`subscribePresentationPoints()`. The host then resolves stationary pointers,\npinned tooltips, and keyboard focus against the painted positions rather than\nthe destination scene.\n\nWhen focus activates inline mark-state geometry, return the resolved scene that\nthe surface paints. The host uses that destination scene for subsequent\npointer resolution while the renderer animates toward it. Returning `void`\nkeeps the base scene as the interaction source and remains valid for renderers\nthat do not resolve alternate scene geometry.\n\nCustom surfaces can reuse the environment-safe focus lifecycle exported from\nthe root and `/universal` entries:\n\n```ts\nconst focusedScene = resolveFocusScene(scene, focus).scene\nconst under = focusedSceneNodes(focusedScene, focus, 'under')\nconst over = focusedSceneNodes(focusedScene, focus, 'over')\n```\n\n`resolveFocusScene` materializes retargetable focus candidates under stable\nkeys. `focusedSceneNodes` returns the ordinary nodes for the requested paint\nplacement. `resolveFocusPresentation(scene, focus, pointer, cursor)` applies\nthat lifecycle and returns renderer-neutral `under` and `over` nodes. Paint\nthem in this order: `under`, the base scene, then `over`. The optional cursor\nargument is the controller state projected into this surface's plot and can\ndrive a crosshair without datum focus. This is the same path used by the SVG,\nCanvas, and React Native surfaces.\n\nThe shared host continues to own runtime updates, responsive sizing, text\nmeasurement, focus resolution, keyboard behavior, built-in tooltips, selection,\nand callbacks. `ChartRendererRenderContext` reports the live `surface` and the\nstable interaction controller instead of assuming an SVG element.\n\nUse `mountChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/renderer`, or the React and\nOctane `/core` entries, to mount a custom renderer. `RenderChartOptions`,\n`ChartSurfaceRenderOptions`, `ChartSurface`, `ChartRenderer`,\n`ChartRendererCapabilities`, `ChartRendererTooltipMotionCapability`,\n`ChartTooltipMotionController`, `ChartTooltipMotionSnapshot`,\n`ChartRendererRenderContext`, `ChartRendererHostCommonOptions`,\n`ChartRendererHostOptions`, and `ChartRendererHost` describe the complete\nboundary.\n\nImport `resolveChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/renderer` when implementing\na host outside the shared adapters. The function returns the effective renderer\nfor prerendering or mounting a scene. It returns the default when every node\nuses that renderer. Otherwise it asks the first non-default\n`ChartLayerRenderer` to compose the ordered layers with the default renderer.\nThe shared DOM host and `createChartRendererAdapter` perform this resolution\nautomatically.\n\nSVG remains available as a renderer implementation:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSvgChartRenderer,\n  svgChartRenderer,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/svg/renderer'\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction createSvgChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  renderSvg?: ChartSvgRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n\nconst svgChartRenderer: ChartRenderer\n```\n\n`createSvgChartRenderer` adapts a `ChartSvgRenderer` into a `ChartRenderer`.\nOmitting the argument uses `renderChartSvg`. `svgChartRenderer` is the shared\npreconfigured instance for renderer-neutral hosts that want the built-in SVG\nsurface.\nPass a `ChartSvgRenderer` as `renderSvg` to the compatibility SVG host or\ndefault framework adapter when only SVG serialization needs to change. Such a\nrenderer should preserve:\n\n- an SVG root discoverable by the host\n- stable `data-ts-key` identities for reconciliation\n- focus-filtered scene groups and data-less guides when chart-owned focus paint is\n  desired\n- the scene coordinate system and accessible name\n\nSee [Custom extensions](./custom-extensions.md#custom-renderers) before\nreplacing the shared renderer.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Rendering and Export\ndescription: Render chart scenes through the default SVG renderer, the optional Canvas renderer, or a custom surface, then export supported output.\n---\n\nTanStack Charts compiles a renderer-neutral scene. The default renderer turns\nthat scene into accessible SVG markup; an optional Canvas renderer paints the\nsame scene through Canvas 2D. Both use the shared responsive, interaction,\ntooltip, keyboard, and runtime host.\n\nUse the task-oriented [Exporting guide](../guides/exporting.md) to choose\nbetween static scene rendering, mounted SVG serialization, and raster output.\n\n## Choose a renderer\n\nRenderer code stays behind explicit entry points:\n\n| Use                              | Import                                                |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Default vanilla SVG host         | `mountChart` from `@tanstack/charts/dom`              |\n| Vanilla Canvas host              | `mountCanvasChart` from `@tanstack/charts/canvas`     |\n| Tween and spring SVG renderer    | `motion` from `@tanstack/charts/motion`               |\n| Renderer-neutral host            | `mountChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/renderer` |\n| Default React SVG component      | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react`                 |\n| Default Preact SVG component     | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/preact`                |\n| Default Vue SVG component        | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/vue`                   |\n| Default Solid SVG component      | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/solid`                 |\n| Default Svelte SVG component     | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/svelte`                |\n| Default Angular SVG component    | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/angular`               |\n| Default Lit SVG element          | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/lit`                   |\n| Default Alpine SVG directive     | `charts` from `@tanstack/charts/alpine`               |\n| React Native SVG component       | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react-native`          |\n| React Canvas component           | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react/canvas`          |\n| React custom-renderer component  | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/react/core`            |\n| Default Octane SVG component     | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/octane`                |\n| Octane Canvas component          | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas`         |\n| Octane custom-renderer component | `Chart` from `@tanstack/charts/octane/core`           |\n\nThe default package and adapter entries do not import Canvas. Applications pay\nfor it only when they import a Canvas entry. Motion is likewise isolated behind\n`@tanstack/charts/motion`. The `/core` adapter entries accept an explicit\n`renderer` without choosing one for the application.\n\nA default SVG host can still compose selected Canvas marks. Import\n`canvasChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/canvas` and attach it to those\nmarks. The default adapter remains the host, and the Canvas painter enters the\nmodule graph through that explicit import.\n\n## React Native adapter\n\nThe React Native adapter is experimental. See\n[Installation](../installation.md#react-native-and-expo) for supported versions,\nverified checks, and native-device validation limits.\n\nThe React Native entry selects its native build through the package export\nconditions and renders the shared scene with `react-native-svg`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  Chart,\n  resolveNativePaint,\n  type NativeChartRenderContext,\n  type NativeChartTooltipRenderContext,\n  type NativePaintContext,\n  type NativePaintResolver,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react-native'\nimport {\n  tooltip,\n  type NativeChartTooltipComponent,\n  type NativeChartTooltipExtension,\n  type NativeChartTooltipProps,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/react-native/tooltip'\n```\n\n`NativeChartRenderContext` is passed to `Chart`'s `onRender` callback.\n`NativeChartTooltipRenderContext` is passed to a custom tooltip renderer.\n`NativeChartTooltipProps` describes the built-in native tooltip component,\nwhose component and extension contracts are `NativeChartTooltipComponent` and\n`NativeChartTooltipExtension`.\n\nUse `resolveNativePaint` as the default `NativePaintResolver`. It resolves\n`currentColor`, Canvas system colors, and CSS-variable fallbacks against a\n`NativePaintContext`. Pass a custom resolver through `Chart` when the\napplication owns additional paint tokens.\n\n## `renderChartSvg`\n\n```ts\nimport { renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/svg'\n\nconst markup = renderChartSvg(scene, {\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n  ariaDescription: 'Revenue increased through the second quarter.',\n  idPrefix: 'revenue',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction renderChartSvg(\n  scene: ChartScene,\n  options: RenderChartSvgOptions,\n): string\n\ninterface RenderChartSvgOptions {\n  ariaLabel: string\n  ariaDescription?: string\n  className?: string\n  tabIndex?: number\n  idPrefix?: string\n}\n```\n\n| Option            | Default  | Meaning                                               |\n| ----------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ariaLabel`       | Required | Accessible SVG name                                   |\n| `ariaDescription` | None     | Escaped SVG `<desc>` content                          |\n| `className`       | None     | Added after the `ts-chart` class                      |\n| `tabIndex`        | `0`      | SVG tab index for direct static rendering             |\n| `idPrefix`        | Empty    | Prefix passed to renderers that generate document IDs |\n\nThe SVG uses `role=\"img\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"chart\"`, a responsive\n`width=\"100%\"` and `height=\"100%\"`, the scene's dimensions as its `viewBox`,\nand an overflow-visible display style. A nontransparent scene background\nrenders as the first rect. All labels escape text and inherit the document\nfont.\n\nFocus-filtered scene groups render hidden until the DOM host supplies focus\nstate. Data-less crosshair guides are also transient and are absent from this\nstatic serialization because no focus or cursor state was supplied. Scene keys\nbecome `data-ts-key` attributes for reconciliation.\n\n## Canvas renderer\n\n```ts\nimport { mountCanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(definition, { tooltip })\n\nconst host = mountCanvasChart(container, {\n  definition: interactiveDefinition,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n})\n```\n\n`mountCanvasChart` has the same definition, sizing, focus, spatial-index,\nkeyboard, tooltip, selection, update, and destroy behavior as `mountChart`.\nThe renderer paints authored focus layers and crosshair guides below or above\nthe base scene on separate canvases, uses the browser device-pixel ratio by\ndefault, and maps pointer coordinates back into the scene.\n\n```ts\ninterface CanvasChartRendererOptions {\n  pixelRatio?: number\n}\n\ninterface CanvasChartSurface<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> extends ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> {\n  readonly element: HTMLDivElement\n  readonly canvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly backgroundCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly focusUnderCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly sceneCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n  readonly focusCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement\n}\n\ninterface CanvasChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> extends ChartLayerRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> {\n  mount: (\n    container: HTMLElement,\n    requestRender: (force?: boolean) => void,\n  ) => CanvasChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ntype CanvasChartHostOptions<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> = Omit<ChartRendererHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>, 'renderer'>\n\ninterface CanvasChartHost<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  update: (options: CanvasChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>) => void\n  getScene: () => ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  destroy: () => void\n}\n\nfunction createCanvasChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  options?: CanvasChartRendererOptions,\n): CanvasChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n\nconst canvasChartRenderer: CanvasChartRenderer\n\nfunction mountCanvasChart<\n  TDatum,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  initialOptions: CanvasChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  runtime?: ChartRuntime<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): CanvasChartHost<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n```\n\nThe surface's `element` is its accessible chart root. `canvas` is the stable\nbase bitmap: chart background plus ordinary scene, without transient focus.\nIt remains suitable for direct `toBlob()` and `toDataURL()` calls and is not\npart of the live visual stack. The live stack is `backgroundCanvas`,\n`focusUnderCanvas`, `sceneCanvas`, then `focusCanvas`. This lets an underlay\npaint above an opaque chart background but below ordinary marks without\nrepainting the stable base bitmap on cursor movement.\n\nA finite, positive `pixelRatio` fixes every backing store at that ratio. An\nomitted value uses `devicePixelRatio`, then `1`; an invalid value uses `1`.\n\n`CanvasChartHostOptions` removes the required `renderer` from the\nrenderer-neutral host options. The returned `CanvasChartHost` owns update,\nscene access, and cleanup. Its optional runtime parameter has the same advanced\nprerender-reuse contract as [`mountChart`](./dom-host.md#signature), including\nruntime ownership on destroy.\n\nUse `canvasChartRenderer` for the shared default instance. Call\n`createCanvasChartRenderer` when the application needs a fixed `pixelRatio` or\nan independently typed renderer instance.\n\nThe server-facing `prerender` step emits a deterministic, named chart shell\nwith five `aria-hidden` canvases: the hidden stable `canvas` base bitmap plus\nthe public `backgroundCanvas`, `focusUnderCanvas`, `sceneCanvas`, and\n`focusCanvas` live layers. It does not attempt server-side pixel painting. The\nbrowser adopts that shell, sizes the backing stores, paints the scene, and\nattaches the shared interaction host. See\n[SSR and Hydration](../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md).\n\nCanvas is an escape hatch for paint-heavy SVG output, not an unbounded-data\nmode. Scene compilation, channel arrays, scene nodes, and interaction points\nstill exist. A default nearest-point lookup remains linear unless the chart\nsupplies a `spatialIndex`; measure the complete pipeline and bound or aggregate\noutput when pixels cannot distinguish the observations.\n\nRenderer-specific tradeoffs:\n\n- Canvas updates raster pixels instead of retaining one DOM element per scene\n  node.\n- Canvas animation crossfades complete frames; SVG animation reconciles and\n  interpolates keyed elements.\n- Curved, polar, and geographic `path` geometry requires browser `Path2D`.\n- Structured `SceneArea.polygons` render directly and do not require `Path2D`.\n- Scene-node `className` values do not create styleable Canvas descendants.\n- Gradients require geometry with measurable bounds.\n- Radial gradients support Canvas fills only. A radial stroke throws rather\n  than changing stroke width under a nonuniform bounds transform.\n\nLinear gradients map their normalized endpoints directly into each node's\nbounds. Radial fills are clipped to the node, then painted in normalized unit\nspace under the node's bounds transform. This preserves SVG\n`objectBoundingBox` behavior, including an elliptical gradient on a non-square\nnode.\n\n## SVG resources\n\n```ts\nimport { renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/svg'\nimport { renderChartSvgWithResources } from '@tanstack/charts/svg/resources'\n```\n\n`renderChartSvg` and the compatible explicit\n`renderChartSvgWithResources(scene, options)` entry both:\n\n- emit declared linear and radial gradients in `<defs>`\n- scope gradient IDs with sanitized `idPrefix`\n- rewrite matching `url(#gradient-id)` paints\n- emit clip paths for scene groups with `clip` bounds\n\nDefault SVG hosts and framework adapters use this behavior without a custom\n`renderSvg`. Use a stable, document-unique `idPrefix`. Gradient coordinates and\nstop offsets are clamped to `0..1` and emitted as percentages. A radial\ngradient defaults to center `(0.5, 0.5)` and radius `0.5`; each omitted focal\ncoordinate inherits the matching center coordinate.\n\nThe React Native adapter emits matching `LinearGradient` and `RadialGradient`\nresources through `react-native-svg`. Its `Chart` generates an `idPrefix` with\n`useId()` unless the application supplies one, then scopes resource IDs and\nrewrites matching paints in the same way as the web adapters.\n\n## `reconcileChartSvg`\n\n```ts\nimport { reconcileChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/reconcile'\n\nconst cancel = reconcileChartSvg(container, nextMarkup, {\n  duration: 240,\n  easing: 'ease-out',\n})\n\ncancel()\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction reconcileChartSvg(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  markup: string,\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions,\n): () => void\n```\n\nThe reconciler adopts a compatible existing root, matches children by\n`data-ts-key`, moves retained nodes into their new order, inserts entries, and\nremoves exits. When a node has no explicit key, same-tag sibling order is a\nfallback identity.\n\nWithout animation, changed attributes and structure commit synchronously.\nWith animation:\n\n- numeric attributes with compatible string structure interpolate\n- entries fade from zero opacity\n- exits fade to zero and are then removed\n- noninterpolable values commit immediately\n- a returned cancellation function stops the current frame loop\n\nThe DOM host calls reconciliation and cancellation for you.\n\nCustom SVG renderers that already own a keyed subtree can reconcile only that\nsubtree without reparsing or walking the surrounding chart:\n\n```ts\nimport { reconcileChartSvgFragment } from '@tanstack/charts/reconcile'\n\nconst cancel = reconcileChartSvgFragment(currentGroup, nextGroupMarkup, {\n  duration: 180,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction reconcileChartSvgFragment(\n  currentRoot: SVGElement,\n  markup: string,\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions,\n): () => void\n```\n\nThe fragment root must keep the same namespace and element name to preserve\nits identity. Otherwise the reconciler replaces it. Child keying, tweening,\nand cancellation match `reconcileChartSvg`.\n\n## Animation options\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartAnimationOptions {\n  duration?: number\n  easing?:\n    | 'linear'\n    | 'ease'\n    | 'ease-in'\n    | 'ease-out'\n    | 'ease-in-out'\n    | ((progress: number) => number)\n  respectReducedMotion?: boolean\n  resize?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n| Option                 | Default      | Meaning                                                |\n| ---------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `duration`             | `240`        | Animation length in milliseconds, clamped to zero      |\n| `easing`               | `'ease-out'` | Named built-in easing or a progress-mapping function   |\n| `respectReducedMotion` | `true`       | Lets a host suppress animation for reduced-motion mode |\n| `resize`               | `false`      | Animates responsive and explicit host size changes     |\n\nOn a definition, `svgAnimation: true` uses `240` milliseconds, `ease-out`, and respects\n`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. A numeric duration is clamped to at least\nzero. A custom easing receives raw progress from `0` to `1`.\n\n`respectReducedMotion` and `resize` are definition policies enforced by the\nhost. Direct\n`reconcileChartSvg(container, markup, animation)` calls run the supplied\nanimation without consulting media queries or render reasons.\n\nHost animation begins only after the initial render. Updates without a scene\nrender do not start an animation; the current animation options apply to the\nnext reconciliation. Responsive and explicit size changes commit immediately\nunless `resize: true`.\n\nStable mark IDs and resolved datum identities are essential for meaningful\ntransitions.\n\n## SVG serialization\n\n```ts\nimport { downloadChartSvg, serializeChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts/export'\n\nconst source = serializeChartSvg(container, {\n  width: 1200,\n  height: 600,\n  includeFocus: false,\n})\n\ndownloadChartSvg(container, 'revenue.svg')\n```\n\nThe subpath exports `serializeChartSvg`, `downloadChartSvg`, and the\n`SerializeChartSvgOptions` type.\n\n```ts\ninterface SerializeChartSvgOptions {\n  width?: number\n  height?: number\n  includeFocus?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n`target` may be the SVG or an ancestor containing `svg.ts-chart`. The serializer\nclones the SVG, adds the XML namespace, removes focus-filtered scene layers\nunless `includeFocus` is true, and resolves dimensions from options, then the\n`viewBox`, then client dimensions.\n\nThe serializer can inline computed `color`, fill, fill opacity, font family,\nfont size, font weight, opacity, stroke, stroke opacity, stroke width, and\nstroke dash array when they depend on inherited font, `currentColor`, or CSS\ncustom properties. Linear and radial resources remain in the cloned `<defs>`,\nand their stop color and opacity receive the same treatment. Keep other\nCSS-dependent resource styling explicit until it is part of that serialization\ncontract.\n\n`downloadChartSvg(target, filename?, options?)` defaults to `chart.svg` and\ndownloads an SVG blob through the target's document.\n\n## Browser image export\n\n```ts\nimport { downloadChartImage, renderChartImage } from '@tanstack/charts/export'\n\nconst blob = await renderChartImage(container, {\n  type: 'image/webp',\n  scale: 2,\n  background: '#fff',\n  quality: 0.9,\n})\n\nawait downloadChartImage(container, 'revenue.png', {\n  scale: 2,\n})\n```\n\nThe browser image functions are `renderChartImage` and\n`downloadChartImage`.\n\n```ts\ninterface RenderChartImageOptions extends SerializeChartSvgOptions {\n  scale?: number\n  background?: string\n  type?: 'image/png' | 'image/jpeg' | 'image/webp'\n  quality?: number\n}\n```\n\nDespite its historical name, `RenderChartImageOptions` supports PNG, JPEG, and\nWebP. `scale` defaults to `2` and is clamped to at least `0.1`. `type` defaults\nto `image/png`.\n\nEncoding support depends on the browser. If the requested encoder is\nunavailable, the browser can return PNG instead, including WebP requests in\nWebKit. Check the returned `blob.type` before choosing a filename or sending\nthe image to a consumer that requires a specific format.\n\nRaster export requires:\n\n- a browser document and window\n- nonzero chart dimensions\n- Canvas 2D\n- successful browser decoding when the source is SVG\n\nThe promise rejects when any requirement fails or Canvas encoding returns no\nblob. `downloadChartImage` defaults to `chart.png`; keep the filename extension\nconsistent with the actual encoded MIME type. The download helper uses the\nfilename you supply and does not rename it after an encoding fallback.\n\nThe raster helpers accept a mounted SVG, Canvas, or mixed chart root, or an\nancestor containing one. SVG is serialized, decoded, and drawn into the export\ncanvas. Canvas uses the stable `canvas` base bitmap directly when focus is\nexcluded. With `includeFocus`, it composites `backgroundCanvas`,\n`focusUnderCanvas`, `sceneCanvas`, and `focusCanvas` in that order. Mixed roots\ndraw every child surface in visual order. `serializeChartSvg` and\n`downloadChartSvg` reject mixed roots and remain SVG-only.\n\n## Mark-level renderers\n\nBuilt-in Cartesian, radial, and composite marks accept a `renderer` option.\nPassing `canvasChartRenderer` opts that mark into Canvas while axes, guides,\nand marks without the option keep the host renderer:\n\n```ts\nimport { areaY, defineChart, lineY, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { canvasChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(denseRows, {\n      x: 'time',\n      y: 'value',\n      renderer: canvasChartRenderer,\n    }),\n    lineY(summaryRows, { x: 'time', y: 'value' }),\n    text(labels, { x: 'time', y: 'value', text: 'label' }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nAdjacent nodes with the same renderer share a layer. Alternating renderer runs\nremain in declaration order, including nested runs inside facets, composites,\nand `polar`. Server output contains one accessible mixed root with\ndeterministic child shells, and the browser adopts those shells. Direct\n`renderChartSvg(scene, options)` calls remain an explicit SVG serialization of\nthe complete renderer-neutral scene and do not run surface composition.\n\nThe universal mark contract stays small:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartMarkRenderer {\n  readonly kind: 'chart-layer-renderer'\n  readonly id: string\n}\n\ninterface ChartMarkOptions {\n  renderer?: ChartMarkRenderer\n}\n```\n\nA renderer that mounts one DOM layer implements the complete composition\ncontract:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartLayerRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>\n  extends ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>, ChartMarkRenderer {\n  compose: (\n    defaultRenderer: ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  ) => ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ninterface UniversalChartLayerRenderer\n  extends UniversalChartRenderer, ChartMarkRenderer {\n  compose: (\n    defaultRenderer: ChartRenderer<any, any, any>,\n  ) => ChartRenderer<any, any, any>\n}\n```\n\nThe first non-default mark renderer supplies the compositor. The built-in\nCanvas renderer can compose normal `ChartRenderer` surfaces and exposes the\nresult as one `ChartSurface`.\n\nMark motion and renderer selection are independent in the authoring API. The\nbuilt-in factories preserve both options, and `createMark` keeps motion as its\nsecond argument and accepts the renderer as its third. The optional\n`motion()` renderer consumes tween and spring policy only on layers it owns.\n`canvasChartRenderer` paints the final mark scene and does not interpret that\npolicy. A host `svgAnimation` can still crossfade complete Canvas frames while\nSVG layers reconcile keyed elements. Changing the layer renderer sequence\nremounts the composition, so that structural update does not animate between\nthe old and new surface layout.\n\n## Custom renderers\n\nThe renderer-neutral boundary consists of a renderer instance contract and\nthe mounted surface it returns:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartSurfaceRenderOptions extends RenderChartOptions {\n  animation?: ChartAnimationOptions\n}\n\ninterface ChartSurface<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly renderer: ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  readonly element: Element\n  readonly layers?: readonly ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[]\n  readonly defaultElement?: Element\n  render: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    options: ChartSurfaceRenderOptions,\n  ) => void\n  clientToScene?: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    clientX: number,\n    clientY: number,\n  ) => { x: number; y: number } | null\n  getPresentationPoints?: () =>\n    readonly ChartPoint<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[] | undefined\n  subscribePresentationPoints?: (\n    listener: (points: readonly ChartPoint<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>[]) => void,\n  ) => () => void\n  paintFocus: (\n    focus: ChartFocusState<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> | null,\n    pointer?: ChartTooltipPosition | null,\n    cursor?: ChartCursorPresentation<TXValue, TYValue> | null,\n    options?: { stateFocus: ChartFocusState<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> | null },\n  ) => ChartScene | void\n  readonly supportsStateFocus?: true\n  destroy: () => void\n}\n\ninterface ChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly id: string\n  readonly capabilities?: ChartRendererCapabilities\n  prerender: (\n    scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n    options: RenderChartOptions,\n  ) => string\n  mount: (\n    container: HTMLElement,\n    requestRender: (force?: boolean) => void,\n  ) => ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n\ninterface ChartRendererRenderContext<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  container: HTMLElement\n  scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  surface: ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n```\n\n`element` is the one accessible, interactive root. `surface.destroy()` releases animation work,\nsubscriptions, and renderer resources. The mounting host owns removal of the\nchart root and cleanup of its interaction listeners.\n\n`layers`, when present,\nlists child surfaces from back to front. `defaultElement` is the topmost\nsurface element owned by the host's default renderer. SVG-oriented\n`ChartRenderContext` callbacks expose that element as `svg` and also include\nthe complete renderer-neutral `surface`. `ChartRendererRenderContext` exposes\nthe complete surface directly.\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartRenderContext<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  container: HTMLElement\n  svg: SVGSVGElement\n  scene: ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  surface: ChartSurface<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n}\n```\n\n| Member                          | Responsibility                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ChartRenderer.id`              | Stable renderer identifier                                                                                                     |\n| `ChartRenderer.capabilities`    | Expose optional versioned services that the shared host injects into extensions                                                |\n| `prerender()`                   | Return deterministic accessible markup for the supplied scene and render options                                               |\n| `mount()`                       | Adopt or create a surface in the container and connect renderer-owned environment observers                                    |\n| `ChartSurface.renderer`         | Refer to the renderer that created the surface; a different renderer object on update replaces the surface                     |\n| `ChartSurface.element`          | Expose the accessible, focusable root used by shared keyboard and focus handling                                               |\n| `ChartSurface.layers`           | Expose ordered child surfaces when this surface composes more than one renderer                                                |\n| `ChartSurface.defaultElement`   | Expose the topmost element owned by the host's default renderer                                                                |\n| `render()`                      | Paint the complete scene and apply accessible name, class, tab index, ID prefix, and optional animation                        |\n| `clientToScene()`               | Optionally convert viewport client coordinates to scene coordinates; the controller returns `null` when omitted or unavailable |\n| `getPresentationPoints()`       | Expose renderer-owned point geometry while a scene transition is active                                                        |\n| `subscribePresentationPoints()` | Notify the host as presentation geometry advances so focus and tooltips remain aligned                                         |\n| `paintFocus()`                  | Paint or clear authored focus layers and guides, then optionally return the destination scene used for subsequent pointer hits |\n| `destroy()`                     | Release renderer-owned animation, observers, listeners, and resources                                                          |\n\n### Rectangle geometry helpers\n\nCustom rectangle renderers can share the built-in corner-fit policy:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  rectCornerRadiiPath,\n  resolveRectCornerRadii,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/renderer/rect'\n```\n\n`resolveRectCornerRadii(corners, width, height)` changes invalid or negative\nvalues to zero and proportionally fits adjacent radii within the rectangle.\n`rectCornerRadiiPath(x, y, width, height, corners)` serializes the same\nnormalized geometry as a stable SVG path. The helper accepts reversed width or\nheight and keeps the tuple in physical corner order.\n\n`requestRender()` asks the shared host to rebuild and repaint on its next\nanimation frame; ordinary requests proceed only when a container-owned width\nor height changed.\n`requestRender(true)` forces the work when renderer state changed without a\nwidth or chart-option change, such as device-pixel ratio or resolved theme\ncolors. Requests made before the same frame are coalesced.\n\nRenderer capabilities are structural so independently bundled package\nentrypoints do not need shared object or symbol identity. A renderer can expose\n`capabilities.tooltipMotion` with protocol `1`; the host creates its controller\nand injects it as `ChartTooltipExtensionContext.motion`. Renderers that omit the\ncapability do not load or run tooltip motion code.\n\nAnimated renderers can expose their current point geometry through\n`getPresentationPoints()` and notify the host through\n`subscribePresentationPoints()`. The host then resolves stationary pointers,\npinned tooltips, and keyboard focus against the painted positions rather than\nthe destination scene.\n\nWhen focus activates inline mark-state geometry, return the resolved scene that\nthe surface paints. The host uses that destination scene for subsequent\npointer resolution while the renderer animates toward it. Returning `void`\nkeeps the base scene as the interaction source and remains valid for renderers\nthat do not resolve alternate scene geometry.\n\nCustom surfaces can reuse the environment-safe focus lifecycle exported from\nthe root and `/universal` entries:\n\n```ts\nconst focusedScene = resolveFocusScene(scene, focus).scene\nconst under = focusedSceneNodes(focusedScene, focus, 'under')\nconst over = focusedSceneNodes(focusedScene, focus, 'over')\n```\n\n`resolveFocusScene` materializes retargetable focus candidates under stable\nkeys. `focusedSceneNodes` returns the ordinary nodes for the requested paint\nplacement. `resolveFocusPresentation(scene, focus, pointer, cursor)` applies\nthat lifecycle and returns renderer-neutral `under` and `over` nodes. Paint\nthem in this order: `under`, the base scene, then `over`. The optional cursor\nargument is the controller state projected into this surface's plot and can\ndrive a crosshair without datum focus. This is the same path used by the SVG,\nCanvas, and React Native surfaces.\n\nThe shared host continues to own runtime updates, responsive sizing, text\nmeasurement, focus resolution, keyboard behavior, built-in tooltips, selection,\nand callbacks. `ChartRendererRenderContext` reports the live `surface` and the\nstable interaction controller instead of assuming an SVG element.\n\nUse `mountChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/renderer`, or the React and\nOctane `/core` entries, to mount a custom renderer. `RenderChartOptions`,\n`ChartSurfaceRenderOptions`, `ChartSurface`, `ChartRenderer`,\n`ChartRendererCapabilities`, `ChartRendererTooltipMotionCapability`,\n`ChartTooltipMotionController`, `ChartTooltipMotionSnapshot`,\n`ChartRendererRenderContext`, `ChartRendererHostCommonOptions`,\n`ChartRendererHostOptions`, and `ChartRendererHost` describe the complete\nboundary.\n\nImport `resolveChartRenderer` from `@tanstack/charts/renderer` when implementing\na host outside the shared adapters. The function returns the effective renderer\nfor prerendering or mounting a scene. It returns the default when every node\nuses that renderer. Otherwise it asks the first non-default\n`ChartLayerRenderer` to compose the ordered layers with the default renderer.\nThe shared DOM host and `createChartRendererAdapter` perform this resolution\nautomatically.\n\nSVG remains available as a renderer implementation:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSvgChartRenderer,\n  svgChartRenderer,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/svg/renderer'\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction createSvgChartRenderer<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  renderSvg?: ChartSvgRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): ChartRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n\nconst svgChartRenderer: ChartRenderer\n```\n\n`createSvgChartRenderer` adapts a `ChartSvgRenderer` into a `ChartRenderer`.\nOmitting the argument uses `renderChartSvg`. `svgChartRenderer` is the shared\npreconfigured instance for renderer-neutral hosts that want the built-in SVG\nsurface.\nPass a `ChartSvgRenderer` as `renderSvg` to the compatibility SVG host or\ndefault framework adapter when only SVG serialization needs to change. Such a\nrenderer should preserve:\n\n- an SVG root discoverable by the host\n- stable `data-ts-key` identities for reconciliation\n- focus-filtered scene groups and data-less guides when chart-owned focus paint is\n  desired\n- the scene coordinate system and accessible name\n\nSee [Custom extensions](./custom-extensions.md#custom-renderers) before\nreplacing the shared renderer.\n"}
